  "observations": [
    "Independent numerical queries accept a natural domain endpoint within the requested stopping error before comparing nearby interior checkpoints. Analytic fast paths, precise inverses and incremental batch policies retain their existing behavior.",
    "Endpoint thresholds are formed before comparison: target <= error, then target >= total - error. Replacing the latter comparison with total - target <= error or a normalized-fraction comparison changes captured floating-point boundary decisions.",
    "The first 63 records cover seven NURBS sources, affine domains, reversals and three coarse precisions, with reordered and repeated fractions. All 3,234 endpoint-tolerance queries match exactly. The full 10,647-query family still exposes unresolved interior checkpoint selection.",
    "The 66 further records include both adjacent floating-point values at each threshold and overlapping endpoint acceptance ranges at 25%, 50% and 75% stopping errors. All 526 exact-threshold and domain-end comparisons match within 1e-9. The complete neighboring-value family remains an ignored strict diagnostic, with unresolved length-rounding ties and interior controls.",
    "Native and Rust sources remain unchanged. A regression also retains affine charts and negative weight gauges while verifying that precise inverses still return interior points.",
    "No early-checkpoint heuristic was introduced. First-checkpoint and binary-prefix substitutions regressed the saved scalar references and were rejected. Coarse global parameter lookup and inherited-sample refinement models still fail adaptive Loft source-clock holdouts."
  ],
